 | Training (s) | Prediction (s) | Settings |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | **svm** | 0.9705 | 8.01 | 2.858 | C=5, gamma=0.02 |\n| 2 | **cnn** | 0.9640 | 15.37 | 0.232 | channels=16, epochs=8 |\n| 3 | **mlp** | 0.9625 | 1.63 | 0.004 | hidden=256, epochs=15 |\n| 4 | **knn** | 0.9500 | 0.01 | 0.965 | k=3 |\n| 5 | **forest** | 0.9480 | 3.32 | 0.033 | trees=100, depth=20 |\n| 6 | **boosting** | 0.9455 | 9.55 | 0.019 | rounds=60, depth=4, eta=0.3 |\n| 7 | **logistic** | 0.9210 | 0.45 | 0.002 | C=0.1 |\n\nThe highest accuracy is **svm** (0.9705, standard error about 0.0038), followed by **cnn** (0.9640). The difference 0.0065, against the fluctuation expected from the 75 images on which the two disagree (about 0.0043), does not reach twice that, so with this many images the order cannot be decided.\n\nThe shortest training is **knn** (0.01 s), The shortest prediction is **logistic** (0.002 s).Times are single-thread CPU times and vary by machine.","markdown":true},"tradeoff":{"type":"plot","library":"Plotly","title":"","xLabel":"Training CPU seconds (log)","yLabel":"Test accuracy","series":[{"label":"","x":[0.0085,1.626,8.0056],"y":[0.95,0.9625,0.9705],"points":false},{"label":"","x":[0.0085,0.4522,8.0056,3.317,9.5484,1.626,15.3691],"y":[0.95,0.921,0.9705,0.948,0.9455,0.9625,0.964],"points":true},{"label":"","x":[0.0021,0.0037,0.2319,2.8576],"y":[0.921,0.9625,0.964,0.9705],"points":false},{"label":"","x":[0.9652,0.0021,2.8576,0.0331,0.0189,0.0037,0.2319],"y":[0.95,0.921,0.9705,0.948,0.9455,0.9625,0.964],"points":true}]},"recall":{"type":"image","src":"assets/mnist-classifiers-recall.png","alt":"Recall per digit. The hardest is 8 (mean 0.920), the easiest is 1 (mean 0.991)"},"hard":{"type":"image","src":"assets/mnist-classifiers-hard.png","alt":"Test images many models got wrong (true → the most common wrong answer, number of models wrong)\nOf 2000 images, all 7 models got 1747 right and all got 21 wrong"}},"artifacts":[{"card":"prepare","output":"subse